WEBVTT

00:02.394 --> 00:04.819
        ♪<i> It seems today</i>
      <i> that all you see</i> ♪

00:04.839 --> 00:07.748
    ♪<i> Is violence in movies</i>
       <i> and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:07.900 --> 00:11.677
     ♪<i> But where are those</i>
 <i> good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.828 --> 00:14.680
 ♪<i> On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.831 --> 00:18.075
 ♪<i> Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.093 --> 00:21.411
     ♪<i> Lucky there's a man</i>
   <i> who positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.430 --> 00:22.855
♪<i> All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:23.006 --> 00:24.264
       ♪<i> Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:30.112
         ♪<i> He's... a...</i>
     <i> Fam... ily... Guy!</i> ♪

00:36.595 --> 00:37.852
         Boy, oh, boy.

00:37.930 --> 00:40.021
       -Is it Friday yet?
           -Tomorrow.

00:40.041 --> 00:42.783
   And actually, in Tasmania,
      it's already Friday.

00:42.935 --> 00:44.376
  I thought you'd be more fun.

00:44.528 --> 00:46.378
       Griffin, you'll be
       very happy to know

00:46.530 --> 00:47.454
    I've finished conducting

00:47.606 --> 00:49.715
    my employee productivity
          evaluations.

00:49.866 --> 00:51.124
     I used a system called

00:51.277 --> 00:52.626
    the Determining Employee
          Advancement,

00:52.795 --> 00:56.037
   Duties, Work-Engagement,
Intelligence-Gains Hourly Test,

00:56.131 --> 00:57.556
         or DEADWEIGHT.

00:57.707 --> 00:58.949
    And my results show you

00:59.042 --> 01:01.134
       to be the brewery's
   least productive employee.

01:01.287 --> 01:03.804
      -So, pack your bags.
           -I'm fired?

01:03.956 --> 01:07.066
 No, you're going on a business
  trip with me as my assistant,

01:07.217 --> 01:09.050
   since you won't be missed
        at the office.

01:09.128 --> 01:10.718
       We're meeting with
   our New Jersey distributor

01:10.738 --> 01:11.737
       in Atlantic City.

01:11.964 --> 01:13.772
            Everyone,
    I'll be away on business

01:13.999 --> 01:15.240
         for a few days
       starting tomorrow,

01:15.467 --> 01:17.076
      so we're bringing in
       a substitute boss.

01:17.303 --> 01:18.819
    I hope he's a hard-ass.

01:18.971 --> 01:20.579
But what if he's wearing jeans?

01:20.806 --> 01:22.973
Hey, guys, my first name is Dan,

01:23.066 --> 01:25.084
          which is what
       you'll all call me.

01:25.235 --> 01:28.328
    Now, who wants to watch
        <i> Ratatouille?</i>

01:28.480 --> 01:30.464
           (cheering)

01:36.322 --> 01:37.321
           (grunts)

01:37.414 --> 01:40.157
   Sorry, that guy over there
           tripped me.

01:40.175 --> 01:41.934
         Mr. Edwards,
    the guidance counselor?

01:42.085 --> 01:44.103
      Yeah, the bullying
   in this school has gotten

01:44.330 --> 01:45.753
     a little out of hand.

01:45.773 --> 01:47.180
      You must be Heather,
          the new girl.

01:47.333 --> 01:48.756
   How'd you know I was new?

01:48.851 --> 01:50.792
         I'm Quahog's
     number three Realtor.

01:50.794 --> 01:52.853
    I really wanted to sell
   that house to your folks,

01:53.005 --> 01:56.031
   but you're in great hands
           with Gil.

01:58.527 --> 01:59.693
          What's this?

01:59.845 --> 02:01.102
Principal Shepherd is directing

02:01.122 --> 02:02.437
an adaptation of Baz Luhrmann's

02:02.531 --> 02:04.364
    <i> William Shakespeare's</i>
      <i> Romeo and Juliet.</i>

02:04.516 --> 02:06.867
    The local Ruth's Chris
 Steak House is sponsoring it.

02:07.019 --> 02:08.685
       I'm playing Juliet.

02:08.704 --> 02:10.295
       Wow. You're Juliet

02:10.372 --> 02:12.189
        in Ruth's Chris's
      Principal Shepherd's

02:12.282 --> 02:14.115
        Baz Luhrmann's
    <i> William Shakespeare's</i>

02:14.135 --> 02:15.801
      <i> Romeo and Juliet?</i>

02:16.028 --> 02:17.210
        Yes, it's great,

02:17.304 --> 02:19.363
     but we're auditioning
       for a new Romeo.

02:19.381 --> 02:20.973
         The parents of
      the boy we cast said

02:21.124 --> 02:23.066
           he needed
 emergency conversion therapy.

02:23.126 --> 02:24.626
Anyway, nice to meet you, Chris.

02:24.794 --> 02:27.062
              ♪ ♪

02:33.061 --> 02:35.687
   I have to be in that play.

02:35.839 --> 02:37.156
            WOMAN:
        Nice hat, dork!

02:37.383 --> 02:41.243
That's not nice, Mrs. Danneman,
   the elderly school nurse.

02:44.147 --> 02:45.889
   Peter, is something wrong?

02:45.908 --> 02:46.981
    We've been here an hour,

02:47.150 --> 02:48.483
   and you've hardly touched
          your penis.

02:48.560 --> 02:50.076
       It's not like you.
       It's getting cold.

02:50.229 --> 02:51.336
          Sorry, guys.

02:51.488 --> 02:53.246
       I just found out
 I have to meet my stupid boss

02:53.399 --> 02:55.507
        in Atlantic City
      for a business trip.

02:55.734 --> 02:57.342
Peter, business trips are great.

02:57.494 --> 03:00.070
    Yeah, haven't you seen
 <i> Cedar Rapids</i> with Ed Helms?

03:00.163 --> 03:02.255
       He plays a salesman
    who goes to a conference

03:02.349 --> 03:03.498
      in the titular city.

03:03.592 --> 03:05.575
      There, he encounters
     three repeat attendees

03:05.669 --> 03:08.094
          who lead him
 on a profound weekend journey,

03:08.247 --> 03:11.765
        equal parts hope
       and self-discovery.

03:12.768 --> 03:15.585
   I memorize Rotten Tomatoes
       movie descriptions.

03:15.604 --> 03:17.587
   You'll have one meeting,
 and then the rest of the time

03:17.606 --> 03:19.923
        -you just party.
      -Party with Preston?

03:20.016 --> 03:21.608
     But he doesn't drink.

03:21.760 --> 03:23.443
  I wish you guys could come.

03:23.537 --> 03:25.204
    Wait a minute. Why not?

03:25.355 --> 03:26.763
   You guys should drive down
            with me.

03:26.782 --> 03:28.189
          -All right!
         -Let's do it!

03:28.283 --> 03:30.116
         <i> Cedar Rapids,</i>
      rated R for drug use

03:30.211 --> 03:32.211
    and mild sexual content!

03:32.362 --> 03:33.954
        I've never been
       to Atlantic City.

03:34.106 --> 03:36.882
    Let's just watch this ad
 from their tourism department.

03:37.033 --> 03:38.700
         <i> ANNOUNCER:</i>
  <i> Welcome to Atlantic City,</i>

03:38.719 --> 03:41.945
  <i> the inspiration for Bruce</i>
 <i> Springsteen's saddest song.</i>

03:41.964 --> 03:45.206
<i> Want to see brown ocean water</i>
<i>stained with gasoline rainbows?</i>

03:45.226 --> 03:46.950
<i> Come on down to Atlantic City!</i>

03:46.969 --> 03:50.287
<i>Love to watch guys with no noses</i>
 <i> fight women with trach holes?</i>

03:50.305 --> 03:51.713
       <i> You're in luck!</i>

03:51.732 --> 03:53.974
    <i> And if you're wondering</i>
 <i> where Taylor Hicks has been,</i>

03:54.068 --> 03:55.292
          <i> he's here!</i>

03:55.385 --> 03:57.827
      <i> In a small lounge</i>
      <i> with a low stage.</i>

03:57.887 --> 03:59.071
        <i> Atlantic City!</i>

03:59.222 --> 04:02.157
  <i> Come flick a lit cigarette</i>
      <i> at a dealer today!</i>

04:02.985 --> 04:04.985
       (insects chirping)

04:06.472 --> 04:09.306
        (British accent):
          "Published by
   the Samuel French Company,

04:09.399 --> 04:12.567
 "New York, copyright this ed.

04:12.661 --> 04:15.570
           MCMLXX."

04:15.589 --> 04:17.923
      -What are you doing?
    -(normal voice): Reading
       <i> Romeo and Juliet.</i>

04:18.116 --> 04:19.316
   We're doing it at school,

04:19.334 --> 04:22.002
      and this girl I like
       is playing Juliet.

04:22.154 --> 04:24.654
I'm going to audition for Romeo.

04:24.823 --> 04:26.372
        There's kissing.

04:26.525 --> 04:28.100
         Chris, listen,
       acting isn't easy.

04:28.327 --> 04:29.977
You're going to need some help.

04:31.939 --> 04:35.256
       See what I'm doing?
      Scarf, a high stool?

04:35.276 --> 04:37.684
           One leg up,
    hands clasped over knee?

04:37.836 --> 04:39.185
   Engaged and in the moment.

04:39.280 --> 04:40.337
  Do you know what this means?

04:40.430 --> 04:42.839
         -You're gay...
     -An acting coach, yes.

04:42.841 --> 04:45.008
        What does a baby
       know about acting?

04:45.027 --> 04:46.860
        Yes, I'm a baby.

04:47.012 --> 04:48.287
   It's hard being youngest,

04:48.438 --> 04:50.622
    always looking for a way
     to distinguish myself,

04:50.774 --> 04:52.532
         to contribute.

04:52.684 --> 04:54.626
        (sobbing softly)

04:55.796 --> 04:57.704
  Stewie, I-I didn't mean it.

04:57.873 --> 05:00.190
        Neither did I.
    That was acting, Chris.

05:00.208 --> 05:02.025
      Wow. You're amazing.

05:02.044 --> 05:04.027
  Do you think you can give me
         some pointers?

05:04.046 --> 05:06.120
   It will be my great honor.

05:06.140 --> 05:08.056
     That was also acting.

05:12.128 --> 05:13.145
Thought I'd swing by work first

05:13.296 --> 05:14.813
   and pick up a case of beer
          for the road.

05:14.890 --> 05:17.482
    Then we're off. (groans)

05:19.728 --> 05:20.894
       Hear him breathe?

05:20.988 --> 05:23.155
       AC's on full blast,
   and he's covered in sweat.

05:23.306 --> 05:24.881
Lois'll be a widow soon, right?

05:24.900 --> 05:26.399
 Yeah, he's circling the drain.

05:26.552 --> 05:28.885
       And let me guess--
       no estate planning?

05:28.904 --> 05:31.479
    Would you guys tell me
  if my car smelled this bad?

05:31.498 --> 05:34.391
      Everywhere I look,
I see another stray french fry.

05:34.409 --> 05:36.835
       Hey, guys? I know
     I'm new to the group,

05:36.986 --> 05:38.411
      but Peter's not here
       to defend himself,

05:38.505 --> 05:41.081
so I don't think it's right for
us to talk about him like this.

05:41.233 --> 05:43.258
         (phone chimes)

05:49.683 --> 05:51.391
            Griffin?
    What are you doing here?

05:52.186 --> 05:53.743
       Oh, hey, Preston.

05:53.762 --> 05:55.670
Why do you have a case of beer?

05:55.764 --> 05:58.673
          Oh. Oh, this?
        Um, uh, samples.

05:58.767 --> 06:00.934
          -For clients.
        -Excellent idea.

06:01.028 --> 06:03.587
       Say, why don't you
         just drive me?

06:03.589 --> 06:06.180
  That way I can be productive
        the entire trip.

06:06.274 --> 06:09.016
   It'll be like<i> Green Book,</i>
      a movie I only saw

06:09.111 --> 06:10.427
     because I believed it
         to be a book.

06:10.429 --> 06:12.278
      Oh, yeah, you know,
   I once tried to read<i> Jaws</i>

06:12.431 --> 06:13.705
       'cause I thought
       it was the movie.

06:13.857 --> 06:16.116
   Couldn't go into a library
      for years after that.

06:16.210 --> 06:18.693
         Guys, listen,
Preston wants to drive with me.

06:18.787 --> 06:21.529
He can't know you're all coming,
  so everyone in the way back.

06:21.623 --> 06:23.273
         I'm not hiding
    in the back of your car.

06:23.366 --> 06:26.200
 Why? There's nothing in there
  except for Lois' jog bras.

06:26.278 --> 06:28.261
 All right, you heard the man!
         Everyone in!

06:30.282 --> 06:31.556
       These are Meg's!
       We've been duped!

06:31.783 --> 06:33.116
         Hop in, boss.

06:33.135 --> 06:34.968
   If I speed, we can make it
         in four hours.

06:35.062 --> 06:37.229
       You'll do a steady
       55 miles per hour,

06:37.398 --> 06:39.398
        and we will stop
   to read historical markers

06:39.625 --> 06:41.474
         -along the way.
       -(Cleveland groans)

06:41.568 --> 06:42.717
    Starting with the Museum

06:42.794 --> 06:44.319
    -of Black Guy Mustaches.
         -CLEVELAND: Oh!

06:56.475 --> 06:57.082
          Some hotel.

06:57.309 --> 06:58.750
  They only had smoking rooms

06:58.902 --> 07:00.234
    and very smoking rooms.

07:00.328 --> 07:03.255
   Check it out, a stack of
   prewritten suicide notes.

07:03.331 --> 07:05.740
     All you have to do is
        sign your name.

07:05.759 --> 07:07.484
   This place has everything.

07:07.577 --> 07:09.744
        I wish there were
       more than two beds.

07:09.838 --> 07:11.321
  I'll just sleep in my chair.

07:11.339 --> 07:12.822
   You sleep sitting up, Joe?

07:12.916 --> 07:14.790
        Yeah, Bonnie puts
      a falcon hood on me,

07:14.792 --> 07:16.083
       and I go right out.

07:17.162 --> 07:20.330
     I'm calm and no longer
       motivated by prey.

07:20.348 --> 07:21.164
           (knocking)

07:21.333 --> 07:22.515
           PRESTON:
       Griffin, open up.

07:22.668 --> 07:24.192
   Guys, hide in the shower.

07:26.338 --> 07:28.095
         Hello, Griffin.
       I'm right next door

07:28.115 --> 07:29.689
   in a slightly larger room.

07:29.783 --> 07:31.283
           Seems like
     an unnecessary detail.

07:31.434 --> 07:33.118
            Here is
   this weekend's itinerary.

07:33.345 --> 07:34.953
  We're working all weekend?!

07:35.104 --> 07:37.864
     Griffin, our New Jersey
   distributor is threatening

07:38.016 --> 07:40.533
       to drop our beer
   in favor of hard seltzer,

07:40.686 --> 07:42.035
     because... New Jersey.

07:42.129 --> 07:43.411
    I need to convince them

07:43.522 --> 07:45.872
      that we are the best
    scumbag beverage around.

07:46.024 --> 07:48.525
    If we lose this account,
      we lose the brewery.

07:48.618 --> 07:50.877
       And then it's time
    to cast open the windows

07:51.029 --> 07:52.879
           and drop to
  the freedom of the pavement.

07:52.956 --> 07:55.715
   I read that in a stack of
   suicide notes in my room.

07:55.867 --> 07:58.201
 See you at 1800 hours, Peter.

07:58.294 --> 07:59.886
         I better shower
     because I have no idea

07:59.980 --> 08:02.147
   how soon or late that is.

08:04.133 --> 08:05.299
       -(shower running)
       -CLEVELAND: Hey!
        -QUAGMIRE: Ah!

08:05.319 --> 08:06.876
      -JOE: What the hell?!
    -PETER: Sorry, I forgot.

08:06.970 --> 08:08.378
             JOE:
   Why are you at half-mast?

08:08.471 --> 08:11.323
             PETER:
 I'm 45, Joe. That's full mast.

08:15.996 --> 08:17.737
  Chris, any good acting coach
          will tell you

08:17.889 --> 08:21.057
   that before your audition,
   it's important to warm up.

08:21.076 --> 08:22.834
        Now let's improv.
       Give me a location.

08:22.986 --> 08:24.077
       Stewie's bedroom.

08:24.229 --> 08:26.079
     Okay, maybe just spend
      another second on...

08:26.231 --> 08:27.672
       Stewie's bedroom!

08:27.899 --> 08:29.508
 Okay, fine. And a profession?

08:29.735 --> 08:30.842
        Acting teacher.

08:30.994 --> 08:32.010
   Again, maybe just give it
          one more...

08:32.161 --> 08:33.253
         Failed actor?

08:33.347 --> 08:34.904
         I got tired of
       playing their game!

08:34.906 --> 08:36.089
       It's okay, Stewie.

08:36.183 --> 08:38.165
        After a few noes,
       these young Brandos

08:38.334 --> 08:39.667
lose a little of their vinegar.

08:39.761 --> 08:42.687
  Tell you what, let's improv
     as Romeo and Juliet.

08:42.839 --> 08:45.190
    You be he, I'll be she.

08:45.417 --> 08:46.599
           (softly):
     Get in. Let's get in.

08:46.752 --> 08:48.918
      I'd like permission
     to go inside, Juliet.

08:49.012 --> 08:50.177
          Hi, Juliet!

08:50.272 --> 08:52.179
           I'm not--
    I'm not there just yet.

08:52.199 --> 08:53.940
      All right, Juliet is
      eluding me a little.

08:54.034 --> 08:56.109
        My transformation
      is not yet complete.

08:56.261 --> 08:58.370
      (takes deep breaths)

09:02.042 --> 09:03.041
          Hi, Juliet!

09:03.268 --> 09:04.376
 Damn it, Chris! I'm not ready!

09:04.603 --> 09:06.694
     But you were standing
         like a girl.

09:06.713 --> 09:08.271
 My bodywork was perfect, yes,

09:08.290 --> 09:10.048
       but I still hadn't
        touched the soul.

09:10.275 --> 09:11.550
      All right, all right,
     even though you're off

09:11.777 --> 09:13.109
  to a rough start, it's okay.

09:13.128 --> 09:16.370
    Even Michelangelo wasn't
appreciated until later in life.

09:16.390 --> 09:18.281
    -Hey, how's Jakey doing?
           -He's good.

09:18.450 --> 09:20.225
  They got him building arches
      over at the Coliseum.

09:20.376 --> 09:22.710
     Big construction job.
       How about Mikey?

09:22.729 --> 09:24.211
       Yeah, he's, um...

09:24.231 --> 09:26.306
    he's been carving dongs
        out of marble.

09:26.458 --> 09:27.983
 You know, something different.

09:30.887 --> 09:33.029
       -(machines chiming)
        -(lively chatter)

09:35.909 --> 09:38.410
   Wow. This place is... sad.

09:38.561 --> 09:40.394
           I'm one of
    the skinniest guys here.

09:40.414 --> 09:42.989
Guys, Preston's coming. Beat it.

09:43.141 --> 09:44.398
      I'm 11 seconds late.

09:44.418 --> 09:46.810
    I'll credit you the time
     in our two-minute break

09:46.828 --> 09:48.253
        in 180 minutes.

09:48.480 --> 09:49.546
          Let's work.

09:50.573 --> 09:52.665
    "Pawtucket Patriot Ale:

09:52.818 --> 09:55.835
      "The Best Carbonated
  Fermented Alcoholic Beverage

09:55.929 --> 09:59.246
 Made from Malted Cereal Grain
  for the New Jersey Market."

09:59.266 --> 10:01.324
             -Zing.
    -That's not very catchy.

10:01.417 --> 10:03.417
      I didn't bring you
  for your opinions, Griffin.

10:03.437 --> 10:04.936
 I brought you for your width.

10:05.088 --> 10:08.231
 Now, stand up while I project
 my presentation on your back.

10:09.851 --> 10:11.943
      (projector whirring)

10:12.095 --> 10:13.503
      This is humiliating.

10:13.521 --> 10:15.188
   I got to figure out a way
       to escape Preston

10:15.340 --> 10:16.356
       and join the guys.

10:16.508 --> 10:18.450
   "Which is why our beer is
         the best beer

10:18.601 --> 10:19.843
     for the Garden State."

10:19.861 --> 10:22.996
   And now for a restorative
     60-second power nap.

10:32.874 --> 10:34.782
   You'll nail this audition,
             Chris.

10:34.801 --> 10:36.209
       Behind you, fellas.

10:36.361 --> 10:38.211
          -Oh, hi, Meg.
        -That's not her.

10:38.363 --> 10:41.598
     All high school theater
 tech girls just look like Meg.

10:44.144 --> 10:46.536
           SHEPHERD:
  Chris Griffin to the stage,
            please.

10:46.629 --> 10:48.438
     Okay, Chris. Go time.

10:50.967 --> 10:54.377
   Curtain rises, lights up,
        a story begins.

10:54.396 --> 10:57.322
     And today our story is
       about a rising star

10:57.473 --> 11:01.234
in Constellation Showbiz Major:
        Chris Griffin.

11:01.328 --> 11:03.052
At the Stewie Griffin Workshop,

11:03.071 --> 11:04.570
          he's studied
      Commercial Technique

11:04.739 --> 11:06.072
     and Acting for Camera,

11:06.224 --> 11:08.424
     and will soon be seen
     in a local news story

11:08.426 --> 11:10.576
          about kids
   who throw stuff at birds.

11:10.671 --> 11:13.396
        Enter... Chris.

11:13.398 --> 11:16.082
  "She doth teach the torches
          to burn..."

11:16.234 --> 11:18.902
    Great! It's fine, Chris.
        The part's yours.

11:18.920 --> 11:20.904
  I got my first-ever response
           on Tinder,

11:20.922 --> 11:22.681
       and I got to make
       this happen now.

11:22.832 --> 11:24.498
    "Are you sure you're not

11:24.634 --> 11:29.929
     a baby pretending to be
    a middle-aged divorcée?"

11:30.023 --> 11:34.508
"Would a baby be wearing a sheer
   chemise from Lane Bryant?"

11:34.528 --> 11:36.361
    Chris, congratulations!

11:36.512 --> 11:37.862
       We did it, Stewie.

11:38.089 --> 11:41.515
       (gasps) Oh, my God,
   I'm going to kiss Heather!

11:41.535 --> 11:43.017
Thanks again for all your help.

11:43.111 --> 11:45.036
           Dear boy,
    I'm not going anywhere.

11:45.146 --> 11:46.871
   My coaching will continue.

11:47.098 --> 11:49.523
        Today's lesson:
  Acting teachers are weirdos

11:49.617 --> 11:51.768
   who always grab your hands
           like this,

11:51.786 --> 11:54.195
        and you can't do
       anything about it.

11:54.289 --> 11:55.714
            No! No.

11:56.883 --> 11:58.425
              No.

12:03.372 --> 12:04.389
        This is awesome.

12:04.540 --> 12:06.799
          Here's to us,
   doing what we normally do,

12:06.893 --> 12:08.301
   but in a different place.

12:09.304 --> 12:12.472
         Griffin. I knew
     I'd find you in a bar.

12:12.624 --> 12:14.624
         I am furious.

12:14.642 --> 12:16.067
      But that doesn't mean
   you shouldn't introduce me

12:16.294 --> 12:17.961
        to your friends
     as a common courtesy.

12:18.054 --> 12:20.296
    Oh, yeah. Uh, Quagmire,
        Cleveland, Joe.

12:20.389 --> 12:23.390
Want to see Sebastian Maniscalco
  with us in the Stardust Room?

12:23.485 --> 12:25.318
      He's that comedian
     who's always startled

12:25.470 --> 12:27.495
         by the pasta
    he takes pictures with.

12:29.324 --> 12:32.475
        No. I'm too busy
    trying to save our jobs.

12:32.494 --> 12:33.752
       Go home, Griffin.

12:33.903 --> 12:36.145
     You are useless to me
       and the brewery.

12:36.164 --> 12:38.405
     You will never amount
     to anything at work.

12:38.425 --> 12:41.259
  Oh, yeah? Well, you'll never
   amount to anything at life.

12:41.486 --> 12:43.486
     You don't know how to
   make friends or have fun.

12:43.505 --> 12:45.838
     You never even tasted
      the beer you sell.

12:45.932 --> 12:48.057
        At least I know
       why it's special.

12:48.994 --> 12:50.009
       Maybe you're right.

12:50.161 --> 12:52.011
    I don't quite understand
           its appeal.

12:52.163 --> 12:53.605
   Well, here's your chance.

12:57.110 --> 12:59.260
 ("The Man in Me" by Bob Dylan
           playing)

12:59.354 --> 13:01.020
              ♪ ♪

13:01.114 --> 13:03.740
   ♪<i> La, la, la, la, la, la,</i>
        <i> la, la, la</i> ♪

13:04.843 --> 13:06.618
 ♪<i> La, la, la, la, la, la, la</i> ♪

13:06.769 --> 13:10.013
     ♪<i> La, la, la, la, la,</i>
     <i> la, la, la, la...</i> ♪

13:10.031 --> 13:13.374
        For the record,
  I've never seen this movie.

13:15.520 --> 13:17.537
        Actors onstage.

13:17.689 --> 13:20.614
        I think you mean,
       company, positions!

13:20.634 --> 13:24.469
     Now, this is the scene
   where Mercutio warns Romeo

13:24.620 --> 13:27.530
  about Juliet's angry brother
             Tybalt.

13:27.623 --> 13:28.865
    Who's playing Mercutio?

13:28.883 --> 13:30.533
  A ten-ounce bone-in rib eye.

13:30.626 --> 13:32.735
           (sizzling)

13:32.737 --> 13:35.296
  Man, Ruth's Chris really has
   their hooks in this thing.

13:35.315 --> 13:37.464
Okay, Chris, move to the right.

13:37.484 --> 13:39.225
         -Stage left.
    -Heather, come forward.

13:39.319 --> 13:41.210
           -Downstage.
       -And to the right.

13:41.229 --> 13:42.803
          -Stage left.
        -Back up, Chris.

13:42.897 --> 13:43.855
        Upstage, Chris.

13:44.007 --> 13:45.139
             -Stop.
           -Stage go.

13:45.233 --> 13:46.732
     Am I scared of Tybalt?

13:46.827 --> 13:49.068
  Yes, but Juliet can't know.

13:49.162 --> 13:50.386
    I'm gonna build on that,
            if I may.

13:50.405 --> 13:51.663
 Ignore that direction, Chris.

13:51.814 --> 13:55.074
 No, Chris, follow the emotion
     and take it further.

13:55.226 --> 13:56.984
      Great note. Chris,
   don't listen to the note.

13:57.078 --> 13:58.244
        Take it further.

13:58.338 --> 13:59.987
           Of course,
   absolutely take it further

14:00.006 --> 14:01.080
 but in the opposite direction.

14:01.232 --> 14:02.248
     Who's in charge here?

14:02.400 --> 14:04.008
     I'm starting to wonder
          that myself.

14:04.235 --> 14:06.827
  If you're trying to drive me
    out of my own production,

14:06.847 --> 14:08.388
     -you've got another...
         -(phone chimes)

14:09.498 --> 14:11.498
     Oh, my first response
       on Farmers Only.

14:11.518 --> 14:13.409
       A divorcée in Ohio
        wants to show me

14:13.428 --> 14:16.095
  her sheer Lane Bryant teddy.

14:16.247 --> 14:17.397
    Fine. The show's yours.

14:18.191 --> 14:20.358
      (seagulls squawking)

14:25.090 --> 14:27.699
Oh, man, my head is killing me.

14:27.850 --> 14:29.350
           (groans)

14:29.369 --> 14:32.370
       Did... did we do
   something bad last night?

14:32.539 --> 14:33.946
     Something really bad?

14:34.099 --> 14:36.499
 Preston texted me at 2:00 a.m.

14:38.044 --> 14:39.193
         What do we do?

14:39.287 --> 14:40.712
       If Preston isn't
     at that presentation,

14:40.863 --> 14:42.455
 the brewery's gonna go under!

14:42.607 --> 14:44.549
            (yawns)

14:45.777 --> 14:47.443
Hotel cribs are always so comfy.

14:47.462 --> 14:49.703
   I wish I knew where to get
      one of these puppies.

14:49.723 --> 14:52.223
    Guys, Preston's missing!
       We got to find him!

14:52.375 --> 14:55.143
  That hooker in the bathroom
  was dead when I found her!

14:55.970 --> 14:57.312
         (phone chimes)

15:09.484 --> 15:11.892
         Okay, Preston's
      not answering texts,

15:11.912 --> 15:13.636
     and the presentation's
         in three hours.

15:13.729 --> 15:15.729
  We got to retrace our steps.

15:15.749 --> 15:17.957
              ♪ ♪

15:21.496 --> 15:23.646
         We've been to
   every strip joint in town

15:23.739 --> 15:25.239
and can't find Preston anywhere.

15:25.258 --> 15:27.241
    We hit Uggoz, with a "Z"
           at the end.

15:27.260 --> 15:29.410
          Jersey Girlz,
     with a "Z" on the end.

15:29.429 --> 15:31.337
     C Sectionz, with a "Z"
           on the end.

15:31.489 --> 15:34.157
    I think we can all agree
     that the "Z" on the end

15:34.175 --> 15:35.934
 takes sexy to the next level.

15:36.161 --> 15:38.603
  And when the "Z" is a little
       tilted on the sign,

15:38.754 --> 15:41.088
           ooh-la-la.

15:42.167 --> 15:43.757
 Hey, do you remember seeing us
           last night

15:43.851 --> 15:45.501
  with a dignified Black man?

15:45.520 --> 15:48.020
 Getting a little tired of you
      punching that word.

15:48.173 --> 15:49.672
       No, just you four.

15:49.691 --> 15:52.008
   But that pilot there said
   he'd pay for my college.

15:52.026 --> 15:53.176
  That doesn't sound like me.

15:53.310 --> 15:54.601
  Two-year community college?

15:54.696 --> 15:57.538
        Oh, yeah, that--
   Yeah, that sounds like me.

16:00.961 --> 16:03.610
I really like working with you,
           Heather.

16:03.630 --> 16:04.796
        Me, too, Chris.

16:04.947 --> 16:06.113
          By the way,

16:06.282 --> 16:08.524
      if you want to go in
     for a real kiss today,

16:08.543 --> 16:10.117
       I won't stop you.

16:10.211 --> 16:11.285
       Places, everyone.

16:11.304 --> 16:13.196
And I want to see acting today.

16:13.214 --> 16:15.181
     No more amateur hour.

16:17.293 --> 16:18.792
          -Oh, Romeo.
 -STEWIE: I don't believe you.

16:18.886 --> 16:20.144
            -Again.
          -Oh, Romeo.

16:20.296 --> 16:21.704
        -Bring it down.
          -Oh, Romeo.

16:21.723 --> 16:23.039
         -Bring it up.
          -Oh, Romeo!

16:23.132 --> 16:25.057
   Can we get a sip of water
       for our actress?

16:25.210 --> 16:27.877
   She's sounding a little...
     (smacks lips) "smacky."

16:27.895 --> 16:29.228
       That's it! I quit!

16:29.322 --> 16:31.480
    I am too pretty and rich
      to put up with this.

16:32.475 --> 16:34.066
         She is rich.
    Her dad owns a bunch of

16:34.202 --> 16:35.384
   Ruth's Chris Steak Houses.

16:35.403 --> 16:37.996
 Stewie, you ruined everything.

16:38.147 --> 16:41.407
  I was finally going to kiss
    a beautiful, nice girl.

16:41.559 --> 16:44.243
        She had my heart
         and I had hers.

16:44.337 --> 16:47.580
 Why must dark forces conspire

16:47.732 --> 16:50.591
  to extinguish love's light?

16:54.088 --> 16:56.997
            Everyone,
   we finally have our Romeo.

16:57.017 --> 16:59.392
           (cheering)

17:00.669 --> 17:02.169
        Thanks, Stewie.

17:02.188 --> 17:03.688
     But what about Juliet?

17:03.839 --> 17:05.023
        Don't you worry.

17:05.250 --> 17:07.859
Ruth's Chris's Stewie Griffin's
     Principal Shepherd's

17:08.010 --> 17:09.101
        Baz Luhrmann's
    <i> William Shakespeare's</i>

17:09.195 --> 17:11.587
      <i> Romeo and Juliet...</i>

17:11.680 --> 17:14.532
    -What was the question?
     -I-I don't remember.

17:19.931 --> 17:21.855
     Hello, I lost my boss,

17:21.949 --> 17:24.267
           so I'll be
your substitute presenter today.

17:24.360 --> 17:26.711
       (giggles) But, uh,
    no watching<i> Ratatouille.</i>

17:26.862 --> 17:28.454
           EXECUTIVE:
     We don't get that joke

17:28.606 --> 17:30.339
   which references something
          from earlier.

17:32.443 --> 17:34.886
             PETER:
  "The Importance of Pawtucket
      Patriot Ale Products

17:35.037 --> 17:37.280
         "in Relation to
 the Greater New Jersey Market,

17:37.373 --> 17:39.640
 as Prepared by Preston Lloyd."

17:44.972 --> 17:46.305
    <i> I've already lost 'em.</i>

17:46.399 --> 17:47.398
        <i> What can I do?</i>

17:47.625 --> 17:49.233
        <i> I need a beer.</i>

17:50.570 --> 17:52.719
       Ah... much better.

17:52.739 --> 17:54.480
   Wait a minute. That's it!

17:54.632 --> 17:56.816
              Look,
you're not gonna understand beer

17:56.968 --> 17:58.467
  with numbers or PowerPoints.

17:58.486 --> 18:00.578
          Beer is good
because it makes you feel better

18:00.655 --> 18:03.397
     and do awesome things
   you wouldn't normally do.

18:03.416 --> 18:05.917
       Beer makes memories
        that will last...

18:06.086 --> 18:07.476
      until you black out.

18:07.495 --> 18:11.172
     And when you forget,
     there are no regrets.

18:13.151 --> 18:14.592
       Beer is courage--

18:14.819 --> 18:18.003
   the courage to moon people
     from a not-moving car.

18:18.098 --> 18:20.414
         Beer helps you
      achieve new heights,

18:20.433 --> 18:22.842
       atop the shoulders
     of unwilling strangers

18:22.994 --> 18:24.160
       in a chicken fight.

18:24.178 --> 18:26.345
       Beer makes you grab
         the brass ring,

18:26.439 --> 18:28.648
         or the taser
   of a casino security guy.

18:30.184 --> 18:31.517
 But if you won't listen to me,

18:31.611 --> 18:34.612
listen to Supreme Court Justice
       Brett Kavanaugh.

18:34.763 --> 18:37.173
          I liked beer.
        Still like beer.

18:37.266 --> 18:40.192
         Beer is great
     because life is hard.

18:40.345 --> 18:42.769
      Don't make it harder
          with seltzer.

18:42.847 --> 18:44.697
           (cheering)

18:44.849 --> 18:46.791
Oh, my God. You're cheering me.

18:47.018 --> 18:48.609
        No, we just saw
     a picture of Bon Jovi

18:48.628 --> 18:50.019
    on the wall behind you.

18:50.112 --> 18:51.295
   But you still won us over.

18:51.447 --> 18:53.022
Pawtucket Patriot Ale will stay

18:53.040 --> 18:55.449
          the choice of
     New Jersey alcoholics.

18:55.526 --> 18:57.468
              ♪ ♪

19:05.036 --> 19:06.644
     Preston! You're alive!

19:06.795 --> 19:09.147
    Yes. And thanks to you,
      so is our company.

19:09.298 --> 19:10.890
 But how are you even standing?

19:10.984 --> 19:14.043
     Peter, I had one sip,
     found it disgusting,

19:14.136 --> 19:15.820
      then watched you get
       totally annihilated

19:16.047 --> 19:17.321
     in three minutes flat.

19:17.473 --> 19:20.474
  I realized only a true drunk
     could save the brewery.

19:20.568 --> 19:22.885
     That's why I sent you
     that text last night.

19:22.904 --> 19:24.220
  I spent the morning enjoying

19:24.313 --> 19:26.146
        all four Monopoly
      railroad properties.

19:26.166 --> 19:27.648
         I love trains.

19:27.725 --> 19:28.891
      I'm on the spectrum.

19:28.984 --> 19:30.367
Why didn't you respond to texts?

19:30.444 --> 19:32.895
Looking at trains. Love trains.

19:33.064 --> 19:35.247
      I also love watching
         an employee go

19:35.400 --> 19:38.551
  from least productive to...
   well, kind of productive.

19:40.346 --> 19:42.680
  Thanks for believing in me,
           Preston.

19:42.849 --> 19:44.407
       Hey, you want to go
        down to the pier

19:44.425 --> 19:46.091
 and watch the bodies float in?

19:46.244 --> 19:47.518
         I'd like that.

19:47.687 --> 19:49.520
              ♪ ♪

19:49.689 --> 19:51.597
       (seagull squawks)

19:51.691 --> 19:53.191
       Ooh, there's one.

19:53.359 --> 19:56.009
 Oh, that bird is going to town
             on him.

19:56.029 --> 19:58.029
     Oh, there's another one
   with no hands and no feet.

19:58.198 --> 19:59.697
    What do you think it is,
            Russians?

19:59.774 --> 20:01.032
      Always the Russians.

20:01.201 --> 20:03.850
       How come the bodies
         are all so fat?

20:03.870 --> 20:05.536
 They're full of water, Peter.

20:05.688 --> 20:07.020
    Is that why I'm so big?

20:07.189 --> 20:08.372
    On account of the water?

20:08.449 --> 20:11.024
          No, Peter.
  You are aggressively obese.

20:11.044 --> 20:12.785
   You have no self-control.

20:12.937 --> 20:14.103
 If you don't change your ways,

20:14.196 --> 20:16.029
      you are going to die
          prematurely.

20:16.123 --> 20:18.274
      (seagulls squawking)

20:18.367 --> 20:20.051
            PETER:
       Oh, look, a lady!

20:20.202 --> 20:23.262
           PRESTON:
  (sighs) Yes, Peter. A lady.

20:31.289 --> 20:32.980
       Here's to my love.

20:33.958 --> 20:36.067
      Oh, true apothecary,

20:36.294 --> 20:37.902
      thy drugs are quick.

20:38.053 --> 20:40.738
      Thus, with a kiss...

20:40.889 --> 20:43.991
        I die. (groans)

20:45.970 --> 20:47.970
     Oh, no, Romeo's dead.

20:47.989 --> 20:50.306
       Now he can't enjoy
   Ruth's Chris Steak House's

20:50.324 --> 20:52.458
          Surf-and-Turf
      Two-for-One Fridays.

20:53.494 --> 20:55.378
      (applause, cheering)

20:56.405 --> 20:57.922
           He did it.

20:58.073 --> 21:00.508
   The son of a bitch did it.